cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use gridcarbon data or clients in your work, please cite the dataset
  snapshot below (it has a DOI and a fixed content), or the API if you are
  citing the live service.
type: software
title: gridcarbon clients
abstract: >-
  Client libraries (Python, TypeScript, MCP) for gridcarbon, a keyless public
  API serving hourly electricity grid carbon intensity in gCO2eq/kWh for 45
  zones: 33 European bidding zones (ENTSO-E), 11 US balancing authorities
  (EIA-930) and Great Britain (NESO).
authors:
  - name: gupeng
repository-code: https://github.com/gridcarbon/clients
url: https://gridcarbon.dev
license: MIT
keywords:
  - carbon intensity
  - electricity
  - grid
  - ENTSO-E
  - EIA-930
  - NESO
  - emissions
preferred-citation:
  type: dataset
  title: "gridcarbon hourly grid carbon intensity, 45 zones — snapshot 2026-09-04"
  authors:
    - name: gupeng
  year: 2026
  publisher:
    name: Zenodo
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22299989
  url: https://gridcarbon.dev
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  notes: >-
    Hourly values 2017-09-11 to 2026-09-04 (GB half-hourly). Production-based,
    generator-terminal, IPCC AR5 lifecycle factors; GB republishes NESO's
    operational figure and is not comparable in level with the other zones.
    Concept DOI for all versions: 10.5281/zenodo.22299988.
    Derived from ENTSO-E Transparency Platform, U.S. EIA and NESO, none of
    whom endorse this work. Method: https://gridcarbon.dev/methodology
